another that beareth witness of me; and I know that the witness which he witnesseth of me is true.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ6Ye sent unto John, and he bare witness unto the truth.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUBut I receive not testimony from man: but these things I say, that ye might be saved.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_He was a burning and a shining light: and ye were willing for a season to rejoice in his light.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ±But I have greater witness than that of John: for the works which the Father hath given me to finish, the same works that I do, bear witness of me, that the Father hath sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And the Father himself, which hath sent me, hath borne witness of me. Ye have neither heard his voice at any time, nor seen his shape.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd ye have not his word abiding in you: for whom he hath sent, him ye believe not.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhSearch the scriptures; for in them ye think ye have eternal life: and they are they which testify of me.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ4And ye will not come to me, that ye might have life.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book*§chapter«first_verse)ªlast_verse/¦verses—„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤text¾I receive not honour from men.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8But I know you, that ye have not the love of God in you.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqI am come in my Father's name, and ye receive me not: if another shall come in his own name, him ye will receive.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkHow can ye believe, which receive honour one of another, and seek not the honour that cometh from God only?¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpDo not think that I will accuse you to the Father: there is one that accuseth you, even Moses, in whom ye trust.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIFor had ye believed Moses, ye would have believed me: for he wrote of me.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBBut if ye believe not his writings, how shall ye believe my words?¦layout ªlast_verse/